course: dictionary
lesson: 830
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Most known asteroids orbit in the asteroid belt» uses belt to mean a long, narrow area of space, not a strip of leather. Clue words such as asteroids and orbit point to space.
explain: Ask yourself what the belt is in this sentence, then look at the words around it. In «A seat belt's lap part goes low across the hips», the words seat and lap show it is a strap that keeps you safe in your seat. In «his belt bulging with weapons», the weapons are tucked into a strip worn around the waist.
explain: Some meanings are informal. Belt can mean to hit hard or to go very fast, so a sentence about someone who belts off down the road is about speed, not a strap. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, and belt is one of them.
fact: A belt is a strip of leather, cloth or plastic worn around the waist to hold up trousers.
fact: A seat belt is a strap in a car, bus or plane that holds you safely in your seat.
fact: The asteroid belt is a long, narrow area of space between Mars and Jupiter.
fact: Informally, «belt» means to hit hard or to go very fast, and a coloured belt in karate or judo shows your level.
exercise: «Most known asteroids orbit in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter.» What is the belt in this sentence? | A strip of leather worn around the waist | *A long, narrow area of space | A seat strap in a car | A fast punch
exercise: «A seat belt's lap part goes low across the hips.» What is a seat belt? | A coloured mark for karate | *A strap that holds you safely in your seat | A moving loop inside a machine | A leather strip for holding up trousers
exercise: In «a belt, a sword, a cutlass, a pair of pistols», what is a belt? | To hit hard | A moving loop that turns wheels | A strap in a bus | *A strip worn around the waist
test: Mia says, «I'll belt to school today.» What does belt most likely mean? | *To go very fast | To buckle a coat | A loop that turns wheels | To hit hard
test: In a factory, «the belt carries the boxes along to the packing room.» What is the belt? | A coloured mark for judo | *A moving loop that turns wheels | A seat strap | A narrow strip of space
exam: Which meaning fits «He wore a black belt in judo, so he had trained for years»? | To hit hard | A strap in a car | A strip of space between planets | *A coloured mark showing your level
